  <div class="pl-cards">
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>FirestoreBackupService.kt — getUserMetaSnapshot() + addArticleToBatch tag extension</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Add <code>getUserMetaSnapshot(): Result&lt;UserMetaSnapshot&gt;</code> that reads <code>users/{uid}</code> once and extracts both <code>isFirstSync</code> and <code>lastSyncTimestamp</code> from the single <code>DocumentSnapshot</code>. Extend <code>addArticleToBatch</code> with a <code>tags: List&lt;ArticleTags&gt; = emptyList()</code> parameter so chunk-batch callers can fold tag writes into the same commit. Add a clarifying comment on <code>MAX_TEXT_SIZE</code> confirming the comparison uses <code>toByteArray().size</code> (efficiency-13 already fixed in code).</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "add", "text": "data class UserMetaSnapshot(val isFirstSync: Boolean, val lastSyncTimestamp: Long?)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "suspend fun getUserMetaSnapshot(): Result<UserMetaSnapshot> = withAuthenticatedUser { user ->" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  val doc = firestore.collection(USERS_COLLECTION).document(user.uid).get().await()" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  Result.success(UserMetaSnapshot(!doc.contains(\"lastSyncTimestamp\"), doc.getLong(\"lastSyncTimestamp\")))" },
          { "kind": "ctx", "text": "}" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "private fun addArticleToBatch(batch: WriteBatch, articleRef: DocumentReference, article: Article)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "private fun addArticleToBatch(batch: WriteBatch, articleRef: DocumentReference, article: Article, tags: List<ArticleTags> = emptyList())" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "  tags.forEach { tag -> batch.set(articleRef.collection(TAGS_COLLECTION).document(\"${tag.itemId}_${tag.tag}\"), tag, SetOptions.merge()) }" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>FirestoreSyncManager.kt — single meta read + chunk-batch tag inclusion</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Replace the two sequential <code>isFirstSync()</code> + <code>getLastSyncTimestamp()</code> calls in <code>syncLocalChanges()</code> with one <code>getUserMetaSnapshot()</code> call. Pre-fetch tags per chunk and pass them as <code>tagsByArticleId</code> to <code>backupArticlesPaginated</code>, eliminating the per-article <code>backupArticle</code> tag-delegation loop that B1 introduced. Net effect: N separate tag commits per chunk collapse to zero (tags are in the chunk commit).</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "val isFirstSync = firestoreBackupService.isFirstSync().getOrNull() ?: false" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "val lastSync = firestoreBackupService.getLastSyncTimestamp().getOrNull() ?: 0L" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "val meta = firestoreBackupService.getUserMetaSnapshot().getOrNull()" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "val isFirstSync = meta?.isFirstSync ?: false" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "val lastSync = meta?.lastSyncTimestamp ?: 0L" },
          { "kind": "ctx", "text": "// pre-fetch tags for chunk, pass to backupArticlesPaginated" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "val chunkTagsMap = chunk.associate { a -> a.itemId to articleDao.getArticleTags(a.itemId).map { ArticleTags(a.itemId, it, null, null) } }" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "firestoreBackupService.backupArticlesPaginated(articles = chunk, tagsByArticleId = chunkTagsMap, onProgress = { ... })" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>ArticleDao.kt — deleteAllTagsForArticle bulk delete</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Add a single-statement <code>DELETE FROM article_tags WHERE itemId = ?</code> method. Replace the <code>forEach { deleteArticleTag(id, tag) }</code> loop in <code>handleRemoteArticleChange</code> with one call. Room executes this as a single auto-transactional SQL statement — N DAO calls become 1.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "add", "text": "@Query(\"DELETE FROM article_tags WHERE itemId = :itemId\")" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "suspend fun deleteAllTagsForArticle(itemId: String)" },
          { "kind": "ctx", "text": "// in handleRemoteArticleChange:" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "val existingTags = articleDao.getArticleTags(remoteArticle.itemId)" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "existingTags.forEach { tag -> articleDao.deleteArticleTag(remoteArticle.itemId, tag) }" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "articleDao.deleteAllTagsForArticle(remoteArticle.itemId)" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <!-- @include callout { "kind": "risk", "title": "Tag-in-chunk-batch updates the B1 characterization assertion (again)", "body": "B1 changed the test assertion from 'firestore.batch() N times' to 'backupArticle() N times'. B2 removes the backupArticle delegation and folds tags into the chunk batch — assertion must update to 'firestore.batch() once per chunk'. Coordinate timing with B1 implementation to avoid a red test-net between the two slices." } -->
  <!-- @include callout { "kind": "warn", "title": "Chunk tag writes do not breach the Firestore rules access budget", "body": "WRITE_BATCH_LIMIT=20 is sized for the marker create/update rule's getAfter() on users/{uid}/articles/{itemId} — one per article, 20 per batch. Tag subcollection writes (tags/{tagId}) have no getAfter() rule check. Adding tag writes to the chunk batch does not increase the document-access count." } -->
  <!-- @include callout { "kind": "info", "title": "efficiency-13 byte-heuristic already correct — no code change", "body": "Both backupArticle() and backupArticlesPaginated() already compare against toByteArray().size, not text.length. B1's addArticleToBatch also uses toByteArray().size. Step 7 adds only a clarifying comment on MAX_TEXT_SIZE; no logic change is made." } -->
